                <pb facs="0785" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.91/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-19T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>141. Your 160, August 11th; 161, August 13th;<anchor n="4" xml:id="d676-f1"/> and
                    162 August 13, keep Department fully and promptly informed all developments
                    matters referred to in these telegrams particularly as to how treaty is received
                    by Persians.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
